The sphere in **(b)** is now immersed in a liquid in a container, as shown in Fig. 2.2.

{{figure:figure_2_2}}

The density of the liquid is $1100\text{ kg m}^{-3}$. The upthrust acting on the sphere due to the liquid is $2.5\text{ N}$. The magnitude of $F$ is unchanged so that the horizontal rod is **not** in equilibrium.

